# Security headers — applied to every route of the SPA (Cloudflare Pages / Netlify).
# Clickjacking protection: block framing by any OTHER origin.
#
# We use SAMEORIGIN / frame-ancestors 'self' (not DENY / 'none') on purpose:
# the trade & landing pages embed the TradingView charting_library in a
# SAME-ORIGIN iframe (/charting_library/). DENY / 'none' would also block our
# own page from embedding it and break the chart. 'self' still blocks all
# cross-origin framing, so clickjacking is fully prevented.
#
# L-04 hardening: X-Content-Type-Options blocks MIME sniffing, Referrer-Policy
# strips path and query from outbound referrers on cross-origin navigation
# (protects wallet/session URLs from leaking to third parties), and
# Permissions-Policy denies browser features the app does not use. HSTS
# already comes from the host, but we set it here too so it is version
# controlled with the site.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(self), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(), publickey-credentials-get=(self), screen-wake-lock=(), sync-xhr=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Team / profile pages: keep OUT of search engines. Viewable and linked on-site,
# but we do not want the site to rank for any individual's name (targeting risk:
# phishing, SIM-swapping). This is the robust layer; each page also renders a
# noindex meta tag. Do NOT disallow these in robots.txt — a crawler must be able
# to fetch the page to see the noindex. Default new profile routes to noindex too.
/about
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
/about-us
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
